These doubts which they raised as opposition to the prophethood of their prophet indicate the extent of their disbelief, obstinacy, and that they are in the utmost ignorance and misguidance. For they are not fit for opposition in any respect, as we have mentioned; rather, they are themselves contradictory and conflicting. For their saying: {This is not but a human being like yourselves who wants to make himself superior over you} establishes that he has intellect with which he schemes against them in order to dominate and lead them, and along with this he needs to be guarded against lest he be followed. So how does this accord with their saying: {He is only a man possessed by madness}? Is this not the utterance of a misguided confused person, whose matter has been turned upside down, whose intention is to repel [the message] by whatever means presents itself, not knowing what he says? God refuses except to manifest the disgrace of whoever opposes Him and opposes His messengers.

